From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmperageOverspend <no@email.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:23:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Shell: a game may run on a host of its own (DmHost<title
 ID>.framework)

The shared app compiles one host into DmShell, from the engine that builds the
shell. A game whose engine differs from it (changed dm/host or dm/gfx sources,
such as a Mac launcher game engine file with an engine.patch) got only its
game framework from that engine, and ran on the shell's host without the
changes.

- build_host.sh / project-host.yml: the whole host (dm/host's compile, the game
  view, the engine side of Play) as an unsigned framework, built from this tree
  with the game's profile as compiled defaults.
- build_ipa_from_nsp.py --shell-host (with --shell-framework) builds it beside
  the game's framework; the manifest names it (gen_manifest.py
  --host-framework, build_ipa.sh DM_HOST_FRAMEWORK). A build without the flag
  removes an older one.
- build_shell.sh embeds the host a manifest names, and refuses a missing one
  or one of another glue version (DMGlueVersion in its Info.plist).
- build_shell.sh takes the host's compiled defaults from the first game whose
  profile this engine has: a game from a game engine file may have its profile
  only in its own host's engine, and gen_build failed when it came first.
- ShellMain.m keeps the app; the engine side of Play moves to ShellGlue.m,
  linked into every host. At Play the app dlopens the game's own host when it
  has one and calls its glue (ShellGlue.h, DM_GLUE_VERSION) instead of the
  built-in one. Other games keep the built-in host.
- The host reads its own tables (swhle, swforce, swnvn) from its own image:
  DM_HOST_IMAGE (__dso_handle) instead of _mh_execute_header, which is the same
  image in an executable.
- front_ios.m: the TV scene's delegate by class, not by name, so a second host
  in the process uses its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the shared app runs a game whose engine differs from the shell's (a game engine file with an engine.patch) on a host built from that engine
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#626
